WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.991
Counterparty Desk answers one question before work starts: who pays whom?

00:00:05.011 --> 00:00:08.313
It grew from a real service-quote misunderstanding.

00:00:08.333 --> 00:00:11.684
Every name and conversation shown here is fictional.

00:00:11.704 --> 00:00:16.056
The offer has NorthWorks paying Loopline one hundred ninety-nine dollars.

00:00:16.076 --> 00:00:20.221
The reply reverses that understanding and explicitly declines.

00:00:20.241 --> 00:00:22.743
Decide gives refusal priority.

00:00:22.763 --> 00:00:28.392
Both directions stay visible, copying stays locked, and the next step is to stop this offer.

00:00:29.120 --> 00:00:33.212
Extract takes me from the refusal to its exact words and author.

00:00:33.232 --> 00:00:35.693
Price links to the original offer.

00:00:35.713 --> 00:00:41.704
These offsets use Unicode code points, so the highlight stays aligned after the compass emoji.

00:00:41.724 --> 00:00:44.648
Repeated wording is checked within the correct message.

00:00:46.120 --> 00:00:49.117
A friendly reply can reverse the deal too.

00:00:49.137 --> 00:00:53.080
Here, great, let us start accompanies the opposite payer.

00:00:53.100 --> 00:00:56.344
The desk shows a counteroffer and keeps copying locked.

00:00:59.120 --> 00:01:05.671
Now I edit an accepted thread locally, changing both quoted prices to two hundred forty-nine dollars.

00:01:05.691 --> 00:01:08.611
Review thread makes three live Clocked calls.

00:01:08.631 --> 00:01:11.459
Decide accepts the same payment direction.

00:01:11.479 --> 00:01:15.031
Fill supplies the sourced terms and acceptance judgment.

00:01:15.051 --> 00:01:20.600
The complete review enables copying a note with quotations, authors, and source positions.

00:01:24.120 --> 00:01:27.382
Here the work is agreed and the price remains open.

00:01:27.402 --> 00:01:31.185
Raw Decide says agreed; Fill returns a null price.

00:01:31.205 --> 00:01:35.682
The local completeness check shows Key terms missing and locks copying.

00:01:35.702 --> 00:01:37.944
Every endpoint changes the review.

00:01:42.280 --> 00:01:46.104
A request for regression reports leaves acceptance open.

00:01:46.124 --> 00:01:49.792
The desk routes it to clarification and keeps the terms note locked.

00:01:51.280 --> 00:01:58.189
The public desk has five real Clocked reviews on fictional threads, with requests and response data to inspect.

00:01:58.209 --> 00:02:02.390
For another thread, run the app locally with your own Clocked key.

00:02:02.410 --> 00:02:04.369
The key stays on the server.

00:02:04.389 --> 00:02:09.018
Source, setup instructions, and the minimal output check are public.

00:02:09.038 --> 00:02:11.968
Open the desk and read the deal before work starts.

